YuriRTC signed-pointer dual-use disclosure

This package contains a signed manifest that identifies an immutable release of
the @advwebrec/grainloading YuriRTC browser transport and its SHA-256 digest. It
is a release-integrity control plane for that dual-use loader. The package does
not contain the private signing key or execute installation scripts.

The referenced loader transports a site operator's hosted web content over
WebRTC and uses a service worker to reconstruct same-origin responses. It is
intended only for legitimate, authorized hosting and access to content. It must
not be used to bypass access controls, monitoring, organizational policy, or
network restrictions without the authorization of the affected users and system
or network owners.

Readable source, build instructions, tests, and deployment documentation are
available at https://github.com/EDUrocks-Group/YuriRTC.

Security and abuse reports may be filed privately with allhands@edurocks.org or
through https://github.com/EDUrocks-Group/YuriRTC/issues.
